Moved the profile flow into its own nested router, managed by `EditProfileFlowScreen`. 

The new flow can be started using `startProfileFlow`:

```
void startProfileFlow({
  @required BuildContext context,
  @required ProfileFlowConfig config,
  @required VoidCallback onFinished,
})
```

For now the ProfileFlowConfig just holds an array of the paths to screens that should be part of the flow, and `escapable`, which lets us control wether or not the user should be able to leave the flow. 

I renamed the source files of the profile screens to use snake_case to be consistent with Dart conventions, and moved them into their own directory at `lib/screens/profile_flow`

